From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:59:33 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8996: add the USB 3.0 controller reset

When LK brings up USB without the QMP PHY (its PHY setup failed, or
the board asks for high speed only), it switches the controller's
PIPE interface over to the UTMI side: PIPE_UTMI_CLK_SEL and
PIPE3_PHYSTATUS_SW in QSCRATCH_GENERAL_CFG stay set when Linux starts.
The dwc3-qcom glue only sets these bits, for
qcom,select-utmi-as-pipe-clk, and with no reset in the node nothing
clears them. A board that uses the QMP PHY then never gets a
SuperSpeed link: as a host the port stays in RxDetect, and as a device
the link stays in SS.RxDetect without falling back to high speed, so
the host sees nothing.

Describe GCC_USB_30_BCR, as msm8998 and sdm630 do. The glue pulses it
at probe, which puts QSCRATCH back in its reset state. Qualcomm's
downstream dwc3-msm driver resets the block the same way, through the
BCR of gcc_usb30_master_clk.

Tested on the Samsung Galaxy Tab S3 (SM-T820) with SuperSpeed enabled
for the board, booted through lk2nd's fastboot mode: QSCRATCH_GENERAL_CFG
reads 0x04 after probe instead of 0x0d, the gadget enumerates on a PC,
and a VL817 hub enumerates at 5000M.

Signed-off-by: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996.dtsi | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996.dtsi
index 1fe0239d4e..c34eae44eb 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996.dtsi
@@ -3167,6 +3167,9 @@ usb3: usb@6af8800 {
 			interconnect-names = "usb-ddr", "apps-usb";
 
 			power-domains = <&gcc USB30_GDSC>;
+
+			resets = <&gcc GCC_USB_30_BCR>;
+
 			status = "disabled";
 
 			usb3_dwc3: usb@6a00000 {
